SCOPE — what shipped (parity with the web source)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Composition  : GlassPanel (faint cyan→purple gradient wash) wrapping a responsive [auto,1fr] layout —
                 (1) car visualization (web <TeslaCarViz model batteryLevel isCharging isLocked isClimateOn
                     sentryMode speed>) reproduced natively as a battery ring + model silhouette + corner badges
                     (charging bolt / sentry shield / climate wind / lock) + motion treatment when moving;
                 (2) four radial gauges (web <RadialGauge>): Battery (%/100), Range (SI→distance pref),
                     Speed (SI→speed pref), Power (charger_power kW / 250);
                 (3) two-or-three metric bars (web <MetricBar>): Battery Level, Estimated Range, and Charge Rate
                     ONLY when is_charging (web `{state.is_charging && <MetricBar.../>}`);
                 (4) four status chips: lock (Lock/Unlock), sentry (Shield), climate (Wind), software (Cpu).
  SI parity    : range read as SI metres, speed as SI m/s, charge_rate as SI metres-per-hour, converted at the
                 display boundary; gauge ceilings expressed in SI (600 mi / 250 mph / 100 mi-per-h) so the percent
                 fill is unit-independent — exactly as the web source documents. battery_level (%) and charger_power
                 (kW) are NOT routed through the unit facade (web parity — rendered verbatim).
  Colour parity: web hex → design token (ADR-006 semantic): CYAN→accent, PURPLE→chartSeriesPower, green #10b981→
                 statusSuccess, amber→statusWarning, red→statusDanger, muted-grey inactive→textMuted. batteryColor
                 (>60 success / >25 warning / else danger), boolColor (lock), sentry/climate/speed/power ternaries —
                 all ported + unit-tested.
  States       : loading (skeleton mirroring the gauge layout) / empty ("No live readings") / error (retry) / data
                 + stale banner+auto-refresh / offline banner. Cached content stays visible while stale/offline/
                 refreshing (web parity — parent keeps last good state). Every state renders real chrome.
  Bindings     : P1/S8 VehicleGaugesSource state-holder seam (no HTTP in the view) — vehicle + state + units +
                 loading/error/connection snapshot, mirroring the web props (VehicleGauges is a presentational leaf
                 fed `vehicle` + `state` and reads useUnits); P1/S9 tokens (Color.TS/Font.TS/TSSpacing/TSRadius/
                 TSMotion) + tsGlassPanel + TSButton + TSFadeIn + TSSkeleton; P1/S10 NSLocalizedString facade
                 (table "VehicleGauges"); P1/S11 view.opened telemetry (slug "VehicleGauges", once + idempotent).
  i18n         : 13/13 web keys reproduced (common.battery/range/speed/power/batteryLevel/estimatedRange/chargeRate/
